{"primaryContentSections":[{"kind":"declarations","declarations":[{"platforms":["Linux"],"tokens":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"struct"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"HeapBatchEncoder"}],"languages":["swift"]}]},{"content":[{"text":"Overview","anchor":"overview","level":2,"type":"heading"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Make the destination with "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/HeapEncoding\/documentation\/HeapEncoding\/HTTPDestinations\/HTTPDestination\/heap(appID:region:plan:backoff:clock:)","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":","},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"which fills in the endpoint, this encoder and its limits:"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"syntax":"swift","code":["let heap = try HTTPDestination.heap(","    appID: appID,  \/\/ the environment's ID, from Heap's project settings","    region: .us,  \/\/ or .eu, where the project's data resides","    plan: plan)"],"type":"codeListing"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The body is a JSON object of content type "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"application\/json"},{"type":"text","text":" with two members: "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"app_id"},{"type":"text","text":", the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"app ID the encoder is made with, without leading or trailing whitespace, and "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"events"},{"type":"text","text":", an array"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"of one track event per record, oldest first. Each event is an object of these members:"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"rows":[[[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Member"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Holds"}]}]],[[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"event"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The event’s "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Event\/name"},{"type":"text","text":", as it is"}]}]],[[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"identity"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The record’s session, its "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"SessionKey"},{"type":"text","text":", as a lowercase UUID string; the record’s own "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"EventRecord\/id"},{"type":"text","text":" the same way when its context has no session"}]}]],[[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"idempotency_key"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The record’s "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"EventRecord\/id"},{"type":"text","text":", as a lowercase UUID string; a redelivered record keeps it"}]}]],[[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"code":"properties","type":"codeVoice"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"The event’s stored properties, flattened; left out when there are none","type":"text"}]}]],[[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"code":"timestamp","type":"codeVoice"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"When the event was tracked, in ISO 8601, in UTC with milliseconds"}]}]]],"header":"row","type":"table"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"The session is the only identifier sent: there is no ","type":"text"},{"code":"user_id","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", which is Heap’s own ID of a","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"user, and no ","type":"text"},{"code":"session_id","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":". Heap makes a user for each identity it hasn’t seen, so its users are","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"sessions. A record with no session (one tracked by a tracker without ","type":"text"},{"code":"Enricher.sessions()","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":") is","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"its own user of one event, linked to nothing: Heap takes no event without an identity. The record’s vendor identifier,","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"trace context and standard context, and any other context value, aren’t sent: Heap keeps no","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"built-in property of a server-side event, so they would sit among the event’s own properties,","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"under names of the encoder’s choosing.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Properties are read through the event’s schema in "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"plan"},{"type":"text","text":", as "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"PropertyReader"},{"type":"text","text":" reads them. A"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Events\/documentation\/Events\/Sensitive","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" value is never sent, whatever the record reveals: the property is left"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"out, and so is an element of an array. Heap takes a number or a string as a property’s value,"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"so an object or array is spread into a property per value it holds, named after its path,"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"joined by "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"."},{"type":"text","text":" ("},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"cart.size"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"tags.0"},{"type":"text","text":"), a boolean is sent as the string "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"true"},{"type":"text","text":" or "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"false"},{"type":"text","text":", and a"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"null"},{"type":"text","text":" is left out."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"A record the encoder can’t write is left out of the request, and the batch’s other records are"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"sent: one whose event and version "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"plan"},{"type":"text","text":" doesn’t describe, one whose event name is over 1,024"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"characters, one with a property Heap reserves or a property name or string value of"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"1,024 characters or more, one whose values flatten to one name, one whose event isn’t"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Encodable"},{"type":"text","text":", one that holds a value JSON can’t, one whose timestamp is outside the years 1 to"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"9999, and one too large for a request ("},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/HeapEncoding\/documentation\/HeapEncoding\/HeapEncodingError"},{"type":"text","text":"). "},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/HeapEncoding\/documentation\/HeapEncoding\/HeapBatchEncoder\/requests(for:)"},{"type":"text","text":" returns them"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"as "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"SkippedRecord"},{"type":"text","text":"s, which "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"HTTPDestination"},{"type":"text","text":" logs and reports on its "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"dropReports"},{"type":"text","text":"."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"identifier":"doc:\/\/HeapEncoding\/documentation\/HeapEncoding\/HeapBatchEncoder\/requests(for:)","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" splits a batch into requests within the encoder’s limit, "},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/HeapEncoding\/documentation\/HeapEncoding\/HeapBatchEncoder\/batchLimit","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" by"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"default, and makes none for a batch with no record it can write, so "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"HTTPDestination"},{"type":"text","text":" sends"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"nothing for it. Heap answers a request it takes with 200 and one it can’t with 400, which"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"HTTPDestination"},{"type":"text","text":" drops and reports with every record of the request. Heap stores an event"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"once per "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"idempotency_key"},{"type":"text","text":" within one identity, so a record sent again under the same session"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"is stored once. A record a store recovers after a relaunch keeps its session, so it is sent"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"under the identity of its first send, and Heap stores it once. The bytes are the same for the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"same records on every run and platform: no whitespace, object members in the order of their"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"names’ UTF-8 bytes."}],"type":"paragraph"}],"kind":"content"}],"metadata":{"role":"symbol","title":"HeapBatchEncoder","symbolKind":"struct","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"struct"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"HeapBatchEncoder"}],"externalID":"s:12HeapEncoding0A12BatchEncoderV","remoteSource":{"url":"https:\/\/github.com\/Tyler-Keith-Thompson\/Traffluent\/blob\/main\/Sources\/HeapEncoding\/HeapBatchEncoder.swift#L66","fileName":"HeapBatchEncoder.swift"},"roleHeading":"Structure","modules":[{"name":"HeapEncoding"}],"navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"HeapBatchEncoder"}]},"schemaVersion":{"patch":0,"minor":3,"major":0},"identifier":{"interfaceLanguage":"swift","url":"doc:\/\/HeapEncoding\/documentation\/HeapEncoding\/HeapBatchEncoder"},"sections":[],"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"The "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/HTTPDestinations\/documentation\/HTTPDestinations\/BatchEncoder","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" of Heap’s server-side bulk track API, so an"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"HTTPDestination"},{"type":"text","text":" can send events to a Heap environment’s "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"POST \/api\/track"},{"type":"text","text":"."}],"kind":"symbol","hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/HeapEncoding\/documentation\/HeapEncoding"]]},"topicSections":[{"title":"Initializers","anchor":"Initializers","identifiers":["doc:\/\/HeapEncoding\/documentation\/HeapEncoding\/HeapBatchEncoder\/init(appID:plan:limit:)"],"generated":true},{"title":"Instance Methods","anchor":"Instance-Methods","identifiers":["doc:\/\/HeapEncoding\/documentation\/HeapEncoding\/HeapBatchEncoder\/requests(for:)"],"generated":true},{"title":"Type Aliases","anchor":"Type-Aliases","identifiers":["doc:\/\/HeapEncoding\/documentation\/HeapEncoding\/HeapBatchEncoder\/Failure"],"generated":true},{"title":"Type Properties","anchor":"Type-Properties","identifiers":["doc:\/\/HeapEncoding\/documentation\/HeapEncoding\/HeapBatchEncoder\/batchLimit","doc:\/\/HeapEncoding\/documentation\/HeapEncoding\/HeapBatchEncoder\/transientStatuses"],"generated":true},{"title":"Type Methods","anchor":"Type-Methods","identifiers":["doc:\/\/HeapEncoding\/documentation\/HeapEncoding\/HeapBatchEncoder\/outcome(of:for:)"],"generated":true}],"relationshipsSections":[{"title":"Conforms To","type":"conformsTo","kind":"relationships","identifiers":["doc:\/\/HTTPDestinations\/documentation\/HTTPDestinations\/BatchEncoder","doc:\/\/HeapEncoding\/s8SendableP","doc:\/\/HeapEncoding\/s16SendableMetatypeP"]}],"variants":[{"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}],"paths":["\/documentation\/heapencoding\/heapbatchencoder"]}],"references":{"doc://HeapEncoding/s8SendableP":{"type":"unresolvable","identifier":"doc:\/\/HeapEncoding\/s8SendableP","title":"Swift.Sendable"},"doc://HeapEncoding/documentation/HeapEncoding":{"url":"\/documentation\/heapencoding","type":"topic","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Send records to Heap as custom events, through its server-side bulk track API."}],"kind":"symbol","title":"HeapEncoding","role":"collection","identifier":"doc:\/\/HeapEncoding\/documentation\/HeapEncoding"},"doc://HeapEncoding/documentation/HeapEncoding/HeapBatchEncoder/init(appID:plan:li